{"At board no. 7, Mr C. W. Sumner (Cambridge) played a Vienna against Mr A. S. Ward (Oxford), and early won a rook, but subsequently had to give up his Q for a second rook. A somewhat featureless game followed, and the adjudicators give the result as a draw." (BCM)} 1. e4 e5 2. Nc3 {... x moves. Source: The Field, 4 April 1896; BCM, May 1896, p198} 1/2-1/2

